+---
+id: dl-001-use-strict-token-traversal-for-json-pointer-resolution
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use strict token traversal for JSON Pointer resolution"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need a standard, deterministic way to resolve a JSON Pointer against an in-memory JSON
+document. Subsequent JSON features will depend on this behaviour.
+
+## Decision
+
+Implement RFC 6901 token traversal directly: the empty pointer selects the whole document, all
+non-empty pointers begin with `/`, and reference tokens decode `~1` to `/` and `~0` to `~` in that
+order. Object tokens select own properties; array tokens must be canonical non-negative decimal
+indices and must name an existing element. All malformed pointers and unresolved tokens throw.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The resolver does not expose prototype-chain values or treat the JSON Patch append token (`-`) as a
+valid array reference. Its result is predictable for JSON values including `null`, `false`, and
+`undefined` is never considered a successful resolution.
